;; Class definitions — 6 new classes
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

 [{:db/ident         :mm/Spec
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Memory
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "Spec"
   :dt/abstract?     true
   :db/doc "Abstract root of the DECLARATIVE family — recipe / pattern / type-of-action / how-to.  Per Phase 2 type-lattice ADR D.1 + D.2.  Concrete subtypes: :mm/Workflow (existing; additively re-parented), :mm/Fn (existing; additively re-parented), :mm/Job (new), :mm/Schedule (new), :mm/EffectSpec (new abstract sub-root).  Specs are TIMELESS + REUSABLE — a Spec can be executed many times; each execution produces an :mm/Activity instance referencing its Spec via :mm.activity/spec."}

  {:db/ident         :mm/Process
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Activity
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "Process"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.process/workflow :mm.process/state :mm.process/runs]
   :dt/abstract?     true
   :db/doc "Abstract supertype of :workflow/Process — multi-step running instance of a :mm/Workflow.  Per Phase 2 ADR D.3.  :workflow/Process becomes a subclass additively via the re-parenting at the end of this file.  Composes with the existing workflow-substrate state-machine via :mm.process/state."}

  {:db/ident         :mm/Job
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Spec
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "Job"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.job/fn :mm.job/payload-shape :mm.job/effect-spec]
   :dt/abstract?     false
   :db/doc "Single-step Spec specifying an action to invoke.  Per Phase 2 ADR D.2.  Re-target from the legacy :job/{Scheduled, Recurring, Task, Triggered} family via the Phase 3 migration tx-fn (sandbar.scripts.migrate-mm-temporal).  Each :mm/Job firing produces a :mm/Run referencing it via :mm.run/job."}

  {:db/ident         :mm/Schedule
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Spec
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "Schedule"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.schedule/target :mm.schedule/recurrence :mm.schedule/timezone
                      :mm.schedule/dtstart :mm.schedule/until :mm.schedule/count
                      :mm.schedule/rdates :mm.schedule/exdates
                      :mm.schedule/source-nl :mm.schedule/source-cron
                      :mm.schedule/next-fire-at
                      :mm.schedule/misfire-policy :mm.schedule/concurrency]
   :dt/abstract?     false
   :db/doc "Recurrence Spec firing a :mm/Workflow or :mm/Job per its target.  OWL-Time + RFC 5545 RRULE aligned per the temporal-substrate arc plan §1.1+§1.2.  Each firing produces a new :mm/Process (target=Workflow) or :mm/Run (target=Job).  Per Phase 2 ADR D.2 + D.8."}

  {:db/ident         :mm/EffectSpec
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Spec
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "EffectSpec"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.effect/initiates :mm.effect/terminates
                      :mm.effect/preserves :mm.effect/preconditions]
   :dt/abstract?     true
   :db/doc "Abstract Spec subtype encoding Reiter-style successor-state axioms as DATA, SHACL-validatable at execution time.  Frame-problem-aware per Phase 2 ADR D.4 (Cyc agent finding: the frame problem WILL bite Sandbar in workflow-step form).  When a :mm/Run of a :mm/Job carrying an EffectSpec completes, sandbar can VALIDATE that the actual tx-data conformed to the declared :mm.effect/{initiates, terminates, preserves} sets + that :mm.effect/preconditions held."}

  {:db/ident         :mm/HookEvent
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Event
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "HookEvent"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.hook-event/lifecycle-position :mm.hook-event/default-severity
                      :mm.hook-event/triggered-by-hook
                      :mm.hook-event/applicable-actor-classes
                      :mm.hook-event/substrate-correctness-criticality]
   :dt/abstract?     false
   :db/doc "Concrete subtype of :mm/Event capturing the corpus-hook event taxonomy authored 2026-05-11 (per decisions/event_as_first_class_type_2026_05_11.md).  Receives the 6 existing :mm/Event instances (:memory.events/{session_start, post_commit, pre_grounding, corpus_audit, pre_tool_use, user_prompt_submit}) via the 2026-05-24 collision-resolution migration tx-fn.  Carries :mm.hook-event/* slots (renamed from the legacy :mm.event/{lifecycle-position,default-severity,...} family).  Rules continue to reference instances of this class via :triggered-by typed edges (no rule-side migration needed; only :dt/type of the referenced instances changes from :mm/Event to :mm/HookEvent)."}

  ;; :mm.event/WorkflowTransition hierarchy per ι.3 design ratification Q.ι.3.9.
  ;; Abstract umbrella + 5 concrete subtypes covering the phase-completion +
  ;; degraded-path + hard-fail emission shapes the orchestrator emits.  Class-
  ;; hierarchical subscription via `:dt/type-isa?` cache enables subscribers to
  ;; listen for ALL workflow events via :mm.event/WorkflowTransition without
  ;; enumerating the concrete subtypes.

  {:db/ident         :mm.event/WorkflowTransition
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm/Event
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "WorkflowTransition"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.workflow-event/process
                      :mm.workflow-event/phase
                      :mm.workflow-event/transition]
   :dt/abstract?     true
   :db/doc "Abstract umbrella for the workflow.transition event family emitted by the ι.3 substrate orchestrator (sandbar.workflow.orchestrate).  Per the ι.3 design ratification §Q.ι.3.9 (memory/decisions/iota_3_substrate_orchestrator_design_ratification_2026_05_26.md).  Carries the common workflow-process context slots (:mm.workflow-event/process, :phase, :transition) inherited by all concrete subtypes.  STRICT Event Substrate ADR compliance — emitted via sandbar.util.event/log! per Keystone ADR D.4; class-hierarchical subscription via :dt/type-isa? cache.  Concrete subtypes: :mm.event/WorkflowSessionOpened (phase/activate completion), :mm.event/WorkflowSessionHandoffAuthored (phase/author completion), :mm.event/WorkflowSessionClosed (phase/finalize completion), :mm.event/WorkflowSessionDegraded (κ P18 bootstrap-fallback engagement), :mm.event/WorkflowSessionFailed (hard-fail per `hard-fail-criteria`)."}

  {:db/ident         :mm.event/WorkflowSessionOpened
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm.event/WorkflowTransition
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "WorkflowSessionOpened"
   :dt/abstract?     false
   :db/doc "Emitted at :phase/activate completion when the workflow.process advances from :session/opening to :session/active via the :session/start transition.  Indicates the orientation ceremony has cleared the live-work threshold.  Per ι.3 design ratification §Q.ι.3.9.  Inherits :mm.workflow-event/{process, phase, transition} from :mm.event/WorkflowTransition."}

  {:db/ident         :mm.event/WorkflowSessionHandoffAuthored
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm.event/WorkflowTransition
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "WorkflowSessionHandoffAuthored"
   :dt/abstract?     false
   :db/doc "Emitted at :phase/author completion when the handoff :mm/Log entity is created.  Indicates the session's narrative-state has been captured + persisted, ready for the linking + finalization phases.  Per ι.3 design ratification §Q.ι.3.9.  Refined further at ι.6 implementation."}

  {:db/ident         :mm.event/WorkflowSessionClosed
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm.event/WorkflowTransition
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "WorkflowSessionClosed"
   :dt/abstract?     false
   :db/doc "Emitted at :phase/finalize completion when the workflow.process reaches the :session/closed terminal :success state via the :session/close + :session/finalize transition chain.  Indicates the session lifecycle has reached canonical closure.  Per ι.3 design ratification §Q.ι.3.9."}

  {:db/ident         :mm.event/WorkflowSessionDegraded
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm.event/WorkflowTransition
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "WorkflowSessionDegraded"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.workflow-event/degraded-reason]
   :dt/abstract?     false
   :db/doc "Emitted when the κ P18 bootstrap-robustness fallback engages — typically `:transition-not-found` per compiled-cache-stale (see observations/workflow_transition_verb_identless_unreachable_2026_05_26.md for the empirical reproduction).  The workflow.process does NOT advance to :session/failed; the orchestrator returns `:degraded? true` to the caller which may retry, fall back to text-protocol, or surface to operator.  Per ι.3 design ratification §Q.ι.3.9 + Q.ι.3.2 (detect-and-fallback per Dan-directive 'we don't want to brick')."}

  {:db/ident         :mm.event/WorkflowSessionFailed
   :dt/type          :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of   :mm.event/WorkflowTransition
   :dt/context       "mm"
   :dt/label         "WorkflowSessionFailed"
   :dt/slots         [:mm.workflow-event/failure-reason]
   :dt/abstract?     false
   :db/doc "Emitted on hard-fail — workflow.process advances to :session/failed terminal :failure per any of `sandbar.workflow.orchestrate/hard-fail-criteria` (:schema-corrupt / :substrate-unreachable-persistent / :phase-timeout / :consecutive-transition-rejects-n).  Per ι.3 design ratification §Q.ι.3.4 (4 hard-fail conditions sufficient for ι.3) + §Q.ι.3.9."}]


