  {:db/ident :mm/Instant         :db/doc "Forward declaration; full definition later — concrete zero-extent temporal point.  OWL-Time `time:Instant` analog.  RARE per Q.D.1 (first-class promotion only when compounding-value criterion met — generalized + reusable / semantic-anchor / Spec-referenced).  Carries :mm.instant/at-time."}
  {:db/ident :mm/Interval        :db/doc "Forward declaration; full definition later — abstract non-zero-extent temporal interval.  OWL-Time `time:Interval` analog.  Concrete subclass :mm/ProperInterval.  Carries Option ε paired-property slots (:mm.interval/begins-at-{instant,time} + :mm.interval/ends-at-{instant,time}) + Allen's 13 typed-edge relations."}
  {:db/ident :mm/ProperInterval  :db/doc "Forward declaration; full definition later — concrete temporal interval with strictly-positive extent (start < end).  OWL-Time `time:ProperInterval` analog (the OWL-Time class explicitly disjoint with `time:Instant` — non-zero extent is the defining property)."}]


